    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0915" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg831"/>

                <head>No. 419.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Valera to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain in Washington</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-02-10"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 10, 1886</date>.
                        (Received February 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Minister Plenipotentiary, in compliance with the order of his
                    Government, has the honor to remit to the honorable T. F. Bayard, for the
                    information of the Government of the United States, the inclosed copy of the
                    Official Gazette, of Madrid, in which is inserted the protocol<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d425-f1"/> concluded between Spain and Germany, by the mediation of
                    His Holiness the Pope, Leo XIII, relative to the sovereignty of Spain in the
                    archipelagoes of the Caroline and Pelew Islands, concluded at Rome the 17th of
                    December of the last year.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JUAN VALERA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
